      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okoboji%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's name was chosen to avoid confusion with Minnesota's Lake Minnetonka, leading to the renaming of Iowa Minnetonka to West Okoboji.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://okobojicity.com/our-community/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Settlers dug a channel between West and East Okoboji Lakes in the 1850s, but it lowered Spirit Lake and raised East Okoboji.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://okobojicity.com/our-community/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers in 1857 had little knowledge of the Iowa Great Lakes Region, marking the beginning of Okoboji's development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
